From: Amphion Runtime <runtime@amphion.local>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:50:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(harmony): let the caller park idle ASR workers

Keep in-run spinning and thread ownership unchanged. Streaming ASR otherwise
leaves its encoder, decoder and joiner pools competing with offline diarization
after their Run calls complete.

Opt-in, because on OpenHarmony `construction_policy` is never null -- the
recognizer always constructs one -- so an unconditional entry here applied to
every session from 0.3.19 onward and cost a chunk's worth of wake-up latency
on every decode. Foreground that is a fair trade. Backgrounded it is not: the
platform confines the app to cores 0-3 at 41% of foreground cycles, where
waking three pools per chunk dominates, and a locked-screen meeting lost 18%
of its transcript with no diarization involved. Parking idle pools also only
reduces a flat load, and flat load was measured not to move device temperature
(see docs/speaker/DIARIZATION_HEAT_DEFAULTS_20261010.md), so the benefit this
was reaching for is small while the regression was not.

--- a/sherpa-onnx/csrc/harmony-scheduling.cc
+++ b/sherpa-onnx/csrc/harmony-scheduling.cc
@@ -89,6 +89,12 @@
 void ConfigureHarmonyScheduling(Ort::SessionOptions *options) {
   const auto *policy = construction_policy;
   if (policy == nullptr) return;
+  // Streaming ASR yields between decode calls. Where another on-device model
+  // wants those cores, parking the pools helps; where nothing does, it only
+  // buys a wake-up on every chunk. In-run spinning is untouched either way.
+  if (policy->stop_idle_spinning) {
+    options->AddConfigEntry("session.force_spinning_stop", "1");
+  }
   if (!policy->allow_spinning) {
     options->AddConfigEntry("session.intra_op.allow_spinning", "0");
     options->AddConfigEntry("session.inter_op.allow_spinning", "0");
